        "opportunity": "buildConfigProjectionBundle unconditionally normalizes the same ProjectConfig twice: once for its normalized result and again through projectConfigForPrompt. Each pass rebuilds the normalized object and traverses, trims, filters, and reallocates every configured rules entry.",
        "impact": "Compile each projection bundle with one normalization pass, eliminating one complete rules traversal and the associated transient arrays and objects on every bundle construction while simplifying the projection data flow.",
        "evidence": [
          "src/core/config-projection.ts:125-134 maps, trims, filters, and reconstructs the complete rules collection during every normalizeProjectConfig call.",
          "src/core/config-projection.ts:382-397 shows projectConfigForPrompt always calling normalizeProjectConfig before compiling prompt fragments.",
          "src/core/config-projection.ts:427-434 shows buildConfigProjectionBundle calling normalizeProjectConfig directly and then calling projectConfigForPrompt with the same raw config, causing the second normalization unconditionally.",
          "src/core/artifact-graph/instruction-loader.ts:332-335 constructs this bundle for artifact instruction loading, so the duplicate work occurs on a production projection path.",
          "The current focused baseline remains green: pnpm exec vitest run test/core/project-config.test.ts test/commands/config.test.ts passed 89 tests, and node bin/xirang.js arch validate --json returned success with no errors or warnings."
        ],
        "recommendation": "Introduce a private prompt-projection compiler that accepts an already normalized config. Keep projectConfigForPrompt as the public raw-config entry point by normalizing once and delegating, while buildConfigProjectionBundle computes one normalized value and passes that same value to the private compiler.",
        "keyDesign": "Separate normalization from prompt compilation with a private function such as compilePromptProjection(normalized, scope). Public projectConfigForPrompt remains API-compatible and delegates after one normalization; buildConfigProjectionBundle stores one normalized result and delegates directly to the compiler. Do not expose a second public normalized-config API or add caching.",
        "preservationConstraints": [
          "Preserve the exported signatures and return shapes of normalizeProjectConfig, projectConfigForPrompt, and buildConfigProjectionBundle.",
          "Preserve exact normalized property presence, values, rule-key last-write behavior after trimming, rule item ordering, duplicate rule items, and empty-key or empty-item filtering.",
          "Preserve prompt fragment inclusion, fragment ordering, line ordering, compiledLines ordering, surface and artifactId values, and canonicalTokenPolicy identity and contents.",
          "Preserve decomposition method and skill names exactly, including their restriction to build, explore, propose, and snack prompt surfaces.",
          "Preserve null-config defaults, architecture depth fallback, git/apply/optimization defaults, string trimming, and omission of invalid or absent optional values.",
          "Do not mutate the input config, introduce persistent caching, change I/O, or alter exception timing for malformed programmatic inputs."
        ],
        "implementationOutline": [
          "Extract the fragment mapping and PromptProjection assembly currently inside projectConfigForPrompt into a private helper that accepts NormalizedProjectConfig and the existing prompt scope.",
          "Change projectConfigForPrompt to normalize its raw ProjectConfig exactly once and pass the result to the helper.",
          "Change buildConfigProjectionBundle to assign normalizeProjectConfig(config) once, return that object as normalized, and compile prompt from it through the helper.",
          "Keep projectConfigForRuntime unchanged because it already normalizes only once."
